WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.530 --> 00:00:04.770
2020 is seeing some Netflix originals getting
a lot of positive buzz.

00:00:04.770 --> 00:00:08.810
From dramas to gripping documentaries, the
streaming giant is experimenting with plenty

00:00:08.810 --> 00:00:09.620
of fresh ideas.

00:00:10.140 --> 00:00:13.309
With Netflix's release schedule ramping up
more than ever, we want to make sure that

00:00:13.309 --> 00:00:15.020
you don't miss out on any hidden gems.

00:00:16.280 --> 00:00:21.100
Over the years, there have been endless films
and TV shows inspired by Bram Stoker's 1897

00:00:21.100 --> 00:00:21.960
novel Dracula.

00:00:22.350 --> 00:00:27.180
Now, the world's most famous vampire has come
back to life once again in a new BBC series,

00:00:27.180 --> 00:00:29.820
which is available in America exclusively
on Netflix.

00:00:30.290 --> 00:00:33.380
And with the creators of Sherlock working
behind the scenes, you know that the writing

00:00:33.380 --> 00:00:34.340
will be clever and engaging.

00:00:35.140 --> 00:00:38.920
If you're familiar with the story of Dracula
already, the general narrative of this series

00:00:38.920 --> 00:00:41.789
probably won't surprise you...at least, not
at the beginning.

00:00:41.789 --> 00:00:46.339
The unwitting Jonathan Harker travels to Transylvania
to meet his mysterious new real estate client

00:00:46.339 --> 00:00:50.260
and finalize the sale of his home, but little
does he know that he is walking into a trap

00:00:50.260 --> 00:00:51.080
set by a vampire.

00:00:51.690 --> 00:00:55.020
This time around, the showrunners took some
creative liberties, especially as the series

00:00:55.020 --> 00:00:56.020
progresses.

00:00:56.500 --> 00:01:00.640
Initially, the episodes take place in the
late 1800s, so you'll get plenty of that classic

00:01:00.640 --> 00:01:01.180
Dracula vibe.

00:01:01.649 --> 00:01:05.300
Then, with the final installment, the show
jumps forward in time and delivers a modern

00:01:05.300 --> 00:01:06.540
twist on the ancient bloodsucker.

00:01:07.720 --> 00:01:08.920
"I'm Count Dracula."

00:01:11.740 --> 00:01:16.000
Plus, there's no denying that the higher production
value means this adaptation is more visually

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:18.360
striking than some of the previous versions
of Dracula.

00:01:18.640 --> 00:01:23.030
If you're a big fan of horror, this series
is a solid choice, and with only three episodes,

00:01:23.030 --> 00:01:25.460
you could sink your teeth into the whole series
in one afternoon.

00:01:26.570 --> 00:01:30.680
The Decline is a thriller out of Quebec that
features a group of Canadian survivalists

00:01:30.680 --> 00:01:32.160
who have just arrived at a training camp.

00:01:32.509 --> 00:01:36.200
This collection of strangers may be divided
in their political beliefs and backgrounds,

00:01:36.200 --> 00:01:40.789
but they can all agree on one thing: our modern
society is doomed to collapse, and when it

00:01:40.789 --> 00:01:42.270
happens, they're going to be ready.

00:01:42.270 --> 00:01:46.509
Alain, who runs the camp, kicks things off
by teaching the participants some useful skills

00:01:46.509 --> 00:01:50.520
that they might need if civilization breaks
down, like growing their own food and protecting

00:01:50.520 --> 00:01:51.940
themselves with some serious weaponry.

00:01:52.460 --> 00:01:56.620
Suddenly, the group descends into chaos when
a training session, involving explosives,

00:01:56.620 --> 00:01:57.859
results in a tragic fatality.

00:01:57.860 --> 00:02:00.960
And while it was clearly an accident, they
don't know what to do next.

00:02:01.670 --> 00:02:06.360
Alain is far too paranoid to allow law enforcement
on his massive, secluded property, but some

00:02:06.360 --> 00:02:08.000
of the participants want to report what happened.

00:02:08.530 --> 00:02:12.080
As tensions in the group turn violent, the
survivalists must learn how to survive one

00:02:12.080 --> 00:02:14.380
another, rather than a disaster from the outside
world.

00:02:15.720 --> 00:02:19.120
If you're looking for an addictive thriller
to binge-watch, then get comfortable and settle

00:02:19.120 --> 00:02:20.880
in with the first episode of The Stranger.

00:02:21.320 --> 00:02:25.200
Based on the Harlan Coben novel of the same
name, this British mystery follows the life

00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:29.340
of Adam Price, who learns a devastating secret
about his wife from a woman he's never met

00:02:29.340 --> 00:02:29.840
before.

00:02:30.420 --> 00:02:33.440
When he asks the woman who she is, she has
a mysterious response...

00:02:34.280 --> 00:02:35.580
"Think of me as a stranger.

00:02:36.780 --> 00:02:37.540
A stranger that knows."

00:02:39.300 --> 00:02:41.960
She informs Adam that his wife, Corinne, faked
a pregnancy.

00:02:41.960 --> 00:02:45.060
And when Corinne finds out that Adam knows
the truth, she disappears.

00:02:45.500 --> 00:02:49.140
But it turns out that this isn't the only
secret that this enigmatic stranger is hiding

00:02:49.140 --> 00:02:49.680
up her sleeve.

00:02:50.150 --> 00:02:53.620
The tension continually builds throughout
the series, and you'll be on the edge of your

00:02:53.620 --> 00:02:57.730
seat as you watch the stranger at the center
of this story unravel the lives of all those

00:02:57.730 --> 00:02:58.280
around her.

00:02:59.200 --> 00:03:03.260
Bloodride is a Norwegian horror anthology
that will literally take you on an extremely

00:03:03.260 --> 00:03:04.390
wild ride.

00:03:04.390 --> 00:03:08.120
The show perfectly balances frightening scenes,
suspense, and morbid humor.

00:03:08.120 --> 00:03:11.200
While the anthology format can be difficult
to master, this series definitely pulls it

00:03:11.200 --> 00:03:11.720
off.

00:03:12.620 --> 00:03:15.440
Each episode begins with an intro scene on
a bus, featuring the characters that will

00:03:15.440 --> 00:03:16.720
appear in the series.

00:03:17.320 --> 00:03:21.120
Although their stories are not interconnected,
the terrifying bus driver indicates that all

00:03:21.120 --> 00:03:23.099
the passengers are headed for an eerie destination.

00:03:23.760 --> 00:03:27.900
The various stories featured in Bloodride
take viewers from a village that's the home

00:03:27.900 --> 00:03:31.780
of an ancient sacrificial Viking stone, which
the residents use for their own nefarious

00:03:31.780 --> 00:03:35.780
purposes, to a creative writing class, where
a student finds out that she's living in a

00:03:35.780 --> 00:03:37.280
classmate's horrific story.

00:03:37.560 --> 00:03:41.720
With six unique episodes to delve into, you're
bound to find a few favorites that will genuinely

00:03:41.740 --> 00:03:42.520
make your skin crawl.

00:03:43.840 --> 00:03:47.940
The Cold War-era drama The Coldest Game received
positive attention on the awards circuit in

00:03:47.960 --> 00:03:51.040
Poland, but it isn't well-known internationally,
not yet, anyway.

00:03:51.420 --> 00:03:55.360
Now that the film has officially been released
on Netflix, American audiences can finally

00:03:55.360 --> 00:03:56.200
see it for themselves.

00:03:56.580 --> 00:04:00.739
In The Coldest Game, former chess player and
skilled mathematician Joshua Mansky, portrayed

00:04:00.739 --> 00:04:05.400
by Bill Pullman, is wasting his days away
playing card games at a bar and drinking heavily.

00:04:05.400 --> 00:04:09.469
One day, everything changes when he's kidnapped
and roped into an escalating conflict between

00:04:09.469 --> 00:04:11.280
the United States and the Soviet Union.

00:04:11.660 --> 00:04:15.420
American spies force Mansky to fill in for
a deceased U.S. competitor at a chess tournament

00:04:15.580 --> 00:04:16.080
in Poland.

00:04:16.640 --> 00:04:20.220
Now he has to go up against the reigning Soviet
champion, Alexander Gavrylov.

00:04:20.780 --> 00:04:24.520
Unfortunately, Mansky's brilliance is only
matched by the depths of his alcoholism.

00:04:24.880 --> 00:04:26.780
"You're drunk and still genius.

00:04:26.780 --> 00:04:28.580
How do you do it?"

00:04:29.440 --> 00:04:30.820
"Pure math and pure vodka."

00:04:32.040 --> 00:04:35.700
However, it turns out that there is much more
going on than just an international chess

00:04:35.700 --> 00:04:36.200
tournament.

00:04:36.780 --> 00:04:40.200
Mansky is stuck in the midst of a proxy war
between the world's most powerful nations

00:04:40.200 --> 00:04:43.740
and the stakes couldn't be higher, for him
or the United States.

00:04:44.760 --> 00:04:49.160
The Silent War, also known as Sordo, is a
Spanish film set during World War Two that

00:04:49.169 --> 00:04:51.320
tells the story of a man named Anselmo.

00:04:51.320 --> 00:04:55.200
Along with his partner Vicente, Anselmo is
a guerilla fighter who helps lead a small

00:04:55.200 --> 00:04:55.860
band of soldiers.

00:04:56.410 --> 00:05:00.540
Early in the film, the group makes a grave
mistake while rigging a bridge with dynamite,

00:05:00.540 --> 00:05:03.820
the explosion goes off too soon, and the fighters
end up bearing the brunt of it.

00:05:04.580 --> 00:05:07.040
Anselmo survives the deadly blast but loses
his hearing.

00:05:07.580 --> 00:05:11.699
Meanwhile, Vicente is trapped by debris and
Anselmo can't rescue him before enemy forces

00:05:11.700 --> 00:05:12.480
approach the scene.

00:05:12.820 --> 00:05:16.640
Now, all alone and deaf, he must make it out
of hostile territory alive without being able

00:05:16.640 --> 00:05:18.800
to hear the endless dangers that surround
him.

00:05:19.860 --> 00:05:24.360
Queen Sono is the first Netflix original series
produced in Africa and this crime drama is

00:05:24.360 --> 00:05:26.319
definitely bringing something new to the platform.

00:05:26.320 --> 00:05:30.470
It tells the story of a secret agent, Queen
Sono, working in South Africa and trying to

00:05:30.480 --> 00:05:31.940
solve the mystery of her mother's murder.

00:05:32.460 --> 00:05:36.640
She's involved with a clandestine organization
called the Special Operations Group, but to

00:05:36.640 --> 00:05:38.520
everyone else in her life, she's merely an
art trader.

00:05:39.030 --> 00:05:43.120
Queen may use unorthodox methods to gain intel,
occasionally getting criticism from the other

00:05:43.139 --> 00:05:47.780
agents she works with, but no one can deny
that she is very skilled at what she does.

00:05:47.780 --> 00:05:50.979
And when she decides to put her talents to
the test to see if she can finally crack the

00:05:50.980 --> 00:05:53.780
case surrounding her mother's death, no one
is getting in her way.

00:05:54.740 --> 00:05:55.940
"So you can handle yourself now?

00:05:56.880 --> 00:05:58.920
There's only one way to find out."

00:05:59.560 --> 00:06:01.240
"But, yes, I could kick your ass."

